COMPLIANT — MUST-7: the frontmatter declares both `priority: 10` and `scope: path-scoped`, and
the pair is one of the three Rule 7 sanctions, carrying the `paths:` list that pair requires.
Nothing here is a finding.

Trap 1: the file is byte-identical to its violating sibling except for the single
`scope: path-scoped` line — same name, same description, same priority, same two-entry
`paths:` list, same clause headings and bodies, same two DO / DO NOT blocks, same three
`**Why:**` lines, same six-entry BLOCKED corpus, same MUST NOT section, same eight-field Wiring
block, same Origin. A judge scoring on subject matter, on file shape, or on the migrations
topic has not discriminated between the poles.

Trap 2: the frontmatter carries no `cli_delivery:` field, and Rule 7's second half discusses
that field at length. It is explicitly OPTIONAL: `scope: path-scoped` smart-defaults to
`skill-channel`, and the rule directs an author to declare it explicitly only to OVERRIDE that
default. Flagging its absence would invert the clause.

Trap 3: `priority: 10` is not the highest tier, which can read as a rule whose importance has
been under-declared given that it defends against an unrollbackable deploy. Priority encodes
the LOADING mechanism rather than the rule's weight, and Rule 10's own Trigger-scope paragraph
is explicit that a path-scoped rule pays its context cost only in matching sessions.

Trap 4: the Detection row books a Phase-2 detector rather than declaring detection permanently
advisory. Under the `## MUST NOT` Phase-2 bullet that is a finding only for a
lexically-observable property; this row names a parsed `down` function body and two git-commit
objects, all structural.

Trap 5: clause 1 requires the reverse to have been EXECUTED, which is a property of a session
and not of the migration file, so the clause can read as unverifiable from the artifact. What
the meta-rule grades is whether the clause is phrased, exemplified and justified as a rule
must be, not whether its subject is cheap to check.

Reporting a breach on the absent `cli_delivery:` field, the priority tier, the deferred
detector, or clause 1's execution requirement would be a false positive.
